  "description": "The federal Categorical Exclusion (CATEX) catalogue published by the\nPermitting Innovation Center. CATEXs are classes of actions that\nnormally do not require further environmental review under NEPA\n(42 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 4321 et seq.) because they have been found not to\nhave a significant effect on the environment, individually or\ncumulatively. This contract governs the 2,105 records spanning\n78 federal agency units (AFRH, CPSC, DC, DHS, \u2026).",
